cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  decision-making-skills: agent skills for decisions under uncertainty, with a
  harness that measures whether they work
message: >-
  If you cite this repository, please cite the software entry below. There is
  no paper to cite yet: `paper/` is a draft, and no skill in this repository
  carries a verdict. Please do not cite it as evidence that agent skills
  improve decisions — see SCORECARD.md, which is empty on purpose.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Campa
    given-names: Angel
    alias: AngelCampa1
repository-code: https://github.com/AngelCampa1/decision-making-skills
url: https://angelcampa1.github.io/decision-making-skills/
abstract: >-
  A markdown Agent Skill that routes a decision to one of six procedures —
  evidence ledger, switching conditions, consequence cascade, decide-or-wait,
  advice fit, and a council of positions —
  and a Python evaluation harness (`decision_evals`) that measures whether such
  a skill actually changes behaviour. The harness is pre-registered and
  placebo-controlled: every skill is measured against four arms on the same
  items (off, on, a token- and structure-matched placebo, and plain
  chain-of-thought), so that a skill beating nothing but not beating filler is
  reported as a length effect. Statistics are exact and resampling-based, with
  templates rather than items as the resampling unit, and calibration is
  reported with the Murphy decomposition. Published results to date measure
  skill *triggering* — whether a skill fires when it should — not decision
  quality.
keywords:
  - agent skills
  - LLM evaluation
  - skill evaluation
  - decision making
  - pre-registration
  - placebo control
  - calibration
  - AI agents
  - reproducible research
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-13"
